abstract: >-
  The CIDOC CRM Periodic Table is a browser-based interface
  for reading and applying the CIDOC Conceptual Reference
  Model together with three of its extensions: CRMsci 3.2
  (scientific observation and measurement), CRMdig 5.0
  (provenance of digital processes) and CRMinf 1.2.1
  (inference and belief). It renders 131 classes and 480
  property entries as a single navigable surface, coloured
  by class family and filterable per model, so that a
  modeller can see a whole model at once instead of paging
  through four separate specification documents.


  Beyond browsing, it offers two forms of modelling support.
  A one-step triple builder admits only the class and
  property combinations licensed by the declared domains,
  ranges and the transitive subclass closure, and reads the
  result back as an English sentence and as instance-level
  Turtle. A multi-step path finder enumerates property
  chains between two chosen classes, ranks them by
  specificity, and marks those that hold only for a more
  specific intermediate class. Because all loaded models are
  merged into one dictionary keyed by code before the
  hierarchy closures are computed, both facilities resolve
  chains that cross model boundaries — for instance that
  CRMdig's D11 Digital Measurement Event is a CRMsci S21
  Measurement, or that a CRMinf property applies to CRMsci's
  S5 Inference Making.


  The interface state is carried in the URL, so any class,
  filter combination or path query is a citable link.
  Everything runs client-side, with no server component.
